Eikos — NOTICE

Our code (inference, serving, data pipeline, training, quantization and evaluation) is released under the MIT
License (LICENSE). The Eikos models are fine-tunes of Qwen base models (Qwen3.5-4B, Qwen3.8-27B; Apache-2.0,
Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud); the model repositories carry the Apache-2.0 license text of the base models.

Models used to build the training data
- GLM-5.3-Flash (MIT, Z.AI): item writing, and blind teacher probabilities at maximum reasoning effort, run by
  the authors on their own infrastructure.
- Qwen3.8-27B (Apache-2.0): item writing and EN<->PT translations.
- Qwen3.5-0.8B (Apache-2.0): candidate solutions for GSM8K answer-verification items.

Third-party data (used for training, with attribution)
- FinEntity — ODC-BY 1.0 — Tang, Y. et al. (2023). FinEntity: Entity-level Sentiment Classification for
  Financial Texts. https://github.com/yixuantt/FinEntity
- TAT-QA — CC BY 4.0 — Zhu, F. et al. (2021). TAT-QA: A Question Answering Benchmark on a Hybrid of Tabular and
  Textual Content in Finance. https://github.com/NExTplusplus/TAT-QA
- GSM8K (train split) — MIT — Cobbe, K. et al. (2021). Training Verifiers to Solve Math Word Problems.
  https://github.com/openai/grade-school-math

Evaluation-only data (downloaded by the suite builders from their sources; never used for training)
- JevBench public items, DecisionBench, CUAD, FinQA, Twitter Financial News sentiment, WCB central-bank stance
  (gtfintechlab; CC BY-NC-SA, evaluation only), FinDVer, RuleArena (MIT), and the general battery tasks
  (MMLU-Pro, RewardBench, ASSIN2, BoolQ, Banking77, CLINC150, LegalBench, XNLI-es, GSM8K test).

Prompt format
- The structured decision prompt (evidence / criterion / lettered options) follows SemIf (MIT),
  https://github.com/theoleecj/semif — credit to its authors.

